{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/120937-mandatory-silly-questions","id":120937,"title":"Mandatory Silly Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-28T08:04:54-07:00","id":120937,"title":"Mandatory Silly Questions","content":"Went through the forums to see if there was a Demon FAQ, but nothing came up, so guessing most folks are adapting to the game easily enough.<br /> <br /> I do not have that luxury, however, so I have a couple of questions regarding things that weren't too clear in the book.<br /> <br /> Q1: With the Embed &quot;Just Bruised&quot;, it doesn't specify whether or not it can be used on the Demon with it, and seems to focus more on &quot;targets&quot;. On the Mend, on the other hand, specifically states the Demon can use that Embed on itself. Is this to say Just Bruised cannot be used on self, or is it to be assumed you can use it on yourself without the same wording as On the Mend?<br /> <br /> Q2: With the Demonic Form Propulsion, &quot;Tether&quot;, it states you can pull another character towards you using the tether, but doesn't seem to specify how fast the target moves towards you. Is it the same speed as the Demon approaching an object he is tethered to, or some other speed rating left unsaid? Given as I assume objects could likely also be pulled with this ability, I feel this needs to be specified, given most objects don't have speed ratings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1353,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","user":"RichE","date":". 05-03-2014, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T05:24:29-07:00","id":124419,"title":"","content":"So no one has answers or even theories on these? I know the thread title might be a turn off, but come on. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T07:57:07-07:00","id":124496,"title":"","content":"I think On The Mend specified the demon itself because there was a lot of questions floating around about it prior to the book's official release, and its wording changed a lot in response to those questions. No reason you cannot use Just Bruised on yourself. <br /> <br /> As for Tether, I'm not sure. I just go by a rule of thumb, and reference the rules for carrying objects by your strength.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T11:08:09-07:00","id":174291,"title":"","content":"question about angel forms it mentions in demonic forms why an angel would have them but the only example i've seen is mr.shivers who had blade hand but that wasn't mentioned in his stats so do angels have demonic form abilities and how many or is it just as many as GodMachine thinks to be efficient such as only giving a psychopomp rivet arm to work with and defend himself rather than waste energy giving a gaurdian or adding additional forms","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3290-godmachine","name":"godmachine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T06:16:07-07:00","id":175962,"title":"","content":"Angels do not need to be given Demonic Form abilities, as these can be accounted for easily under the Ephemeral Creature rules found in the rear GMC rules update. To answer your questions in this vein, to represent an Angel with &quot;Rivet Arm&quot; you would give them the &quot;Blast Numina&quot; or a &quot;gun hand&quot;. It says that an Ephemeral Creature does bashing damage with its attacks unless its nature calls for lethal. If you, as the storyteller, have made the decision that the Angel has a &quot;knife&quot; for a hand, then he would do lethal damage with his basic attacks. If he has a gun for a hand, he would have the range of a similar weapon and do lethal on his attacks. (Though a ranged weapon might be better suited to the &quot;Blast&quot; Numina)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T12:50:57-07:00","id":178141,"title":"","content":"You're the ST. If you think a form ability or a embed would be cool for an angel you're welcome to convert it into a Numina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2037-iceix","name":"IceIX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T13:57:25-07:00","id":178230,"title":"","content":"The simple fact of the matter is that spirits use Influences and Numina for most everything. Just make a Numina or Influence that works like whatever Embed, Exploit, or Form ability you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T14:01:02-07:00","id":178233,"title":"","content":"Angels explicitly can't perform Exploits.<br /> <br /> You can take any Embed usually and just give that as a Numina, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T14:07:48-07:00","id":178237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/120937-mandatory-silly-questions?p=178233#post178233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Angels explicitly can't perform Exploits.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>As Exploits</i>, it should be noted, because if it was actually &quot;no Exploit effect can be replicated by angelic Numina&quot; then that would be bizarre and contradictory in light of things like Possession, Raise Dead, and Force Relationship replicating basic Manifestation Effects, Influences, and explicitly-angel-viable Numina.<br /> <br /> They just don't arrive at those effects by routing additional energy through rote-accessed subroutines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T10:06:22-07:00","id":187219,"title":"","content":"Can Angels sense Aether? In the core book is seems to imply that Aether sensing is a Demon/Crypid only thing. but on Flowers the text mentions Angels sensing Aether flares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1283-duthuras","name":"Duthuras","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T13:24:18-07:00","id":187359,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this has been covered elsewhere - but how do demons find eachother? This is the one thing I don't get - after the fall, the only semi-reliable method of detecting I can see within the system is by using an allied stigmatics omen-sensing powers - and this is problematic at best. I have a bit of a problem imagining the following conversation.<br /> <br /> A. I suspect you are a demon.<br /> B Yes - I am.<br /> <br /> Maybe something more along the lines of a multi-lingual proposition.<br /> <br /> A. Bist du uno diablo?<br /> B. Moi? Veilleicht - come sabes?<br /> <br /> Some kind of linguistic sounding board? Even this is rife with risk for a renegade so far behind enemy lines.<br /> <br /> Can't imagine it happening - as regularly and often as it must for any sense of a society/alliance/organisation. I must be missing something, no?<br /> <br /> hoodedclaw","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T13:51:22-07:00","id":187388,"title":"","content":"In the SAS included in the game, Comrade West speaks to the player characters in an obscure foreign language (I think) when he first greets them. IIRC, that sort of thing is one of the best ways to identify a Demon, and by picking a weird language that they can fluently respond in, it provides an easy way for Demons to acknowledge eachother.<br /> <br /> Since they have the poker face, they're not at risk of unwittingly displaying their comprehension of the statement in their behavior unless they decide to, so you can't catch another Demon based on their reaction to your quick bit of Tagalog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T14:24:35-07:00","id":187409,"title":"","content":"The other major way of knowing other demons are around will probably be sensing their use of Aether, but that's far less exact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T19:32:42-07:00","id":187595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hoodedclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/120937-mandatory-silly-questions?p=187359#post187359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if this has been covered elsewhere - but how do demons find eachother?</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons posses aetheric resonance, based on their premium as per pg184. If another unchained spends a point of aether, they can sense other Demons within a specific radius, though they can't pinpoint the location. One more reason to stick tight to densely populated cities...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T20:02:20-07:00","id":187605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Duthuras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/120937-mandatory-silly-questions?p=187219#post187219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Angels sense Aether? In the core book is seems to imply that Aether sensing is a Demon/Crypid only thing. but on Flowers the text mentions Angels sensing Aether flares.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's the text from Flowers that I think you're talking about, I'll just point out that there's a difference between not being able to see hydrogen atoms and not noticing an exploding H-bomb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T11:29:36-07:00","id":188825,"title":"","content":"Very silly question here: when you Instal a gadget with a power, do you lose that power as is and only have the Gadget (like encoding a Rote into a Grimoire)? Or do you still have access to the power as well? I was under the impression that you lost the power, but rereading the Gadget section, i don't see that anywhere. Plus, losing the power was specifically mentioned in the Demonic Form gadgets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T14:51:06-07:00","id":188936,"title":"","content":"You don't, unless it's a Demonic Form gadget.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T16:12:57-07:00","id":188951,"title":"","content":"On the plus side, Form Gadgets gives you wiiiiiings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T13:33:53-07:00","id":189609,"title":"","content":"Reading the section on building Gadgets in the core Demon book, it says it requires a <i>dot</i> of Willpower to cement the Gadget, otherwise it fades at the end of the scene. However, after reading <i>Flowers of Hell</i>, I got the impression that Gadgets are a pretty common form of currency among the Unchained.<br /> <br /> Did I miss something vital or is the 1 Experience needed to recover the spent Willpower considered trivial these days (in which case, I wouldn't be surprised to see the number of Kindred Embraced explode)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The Man and the Beast are having an amiable picnic in that Savage\u2019s head. It\u2019s rather disturbing.&quot; <i>- Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle, pg. 22</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/145-jsm3050","name":"JSM3050","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T13:41:20-07:00","id":189615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JSM3050</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/120937-mandatory-silly-questions?p=189609#post189609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I miss something vital or is the 1 Experience needed to recover the spent Willpower considered trivial these days</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the price of a single-dot Merit. It's not difficult to earn at least half that cost over the course of a single session.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (in which case, I wouldn't be surprised to see the number of Kindred Embraced explode)? </div> </div> </div>Blood and Smoke's rules for the Embrace now use a Humanity dot as the cost and this is a rather silly conclusion to jump to besides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}